  "summary": "safeGit now returns a { code, stdout, stderr } object instead of the stdout string, and it no longer throws when git fails. index.ts also exports the new GitResult type.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "packages/core/src/safe-git.ts",
      "line_number": 10,
      "line_end": 17,
      "title": "safeGit return shape change breaks both CLI callers",
      "description": "safeGit now returns a GitResult object and no longer throws. currentBranch in packages/cli/src/branch.ts:7 and changedFiles in packages/cli/src/status.ts:7 still call string methods on that result and rely on a throw. In currentBranch, trim throws a TypeError and the catch returns null, so main.ts always exits early. In changedFiles, split throws a TypeError, and failed git commands no longer reach callers as errors. Update currentBranch to return null when code is not 0 and otherwise trim stdout. Update changedFiles to check code and split stdout.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:return-shape-contract-break",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "safeGit now returns a GitResult object and no longer throws. currentBranch in packages/cli/src/branch.ts:7 and changedFiles in packages/cli/src/status.ts:7 still call string methods on that result and rely on a throw.",
      "consequence": "In currentBranch, trim throws a TypeError and the catch returns null, so main.ts always exits early. In changedFiles, split throws a TypeError, and failed git commands no longer reach callers as errors.",
      "fix": "Update currentBranch to return null when code is not 0 and otherwise trim stdout. Update changedFiles to check code and split stdout."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "file_path": "packages/core/src/safe-git.ts",
      "line_number": 13,
      "line_end": 16,
      "title": "No test covers the new safeGit result and error path",
      "description": "safeGit gained a new return shape and a catch branch that maps errors to an exit code. No test in this change exercises either path. A test calling currentBranch or changedFiles would have caught the broken callers before the push. Add tests that call safeGit with a succeeding and a failing git command and check code, stdout and stderr.",
